# REGRESSION — the liveness walker must see uses inside `unsafe:` and a NAMED SCOPE.
#
# `walk_stmt` (src/ir/lowering/liveness.rs) handled 10 of 29 `Stmt` forms and
# swept 19 into `_ => {}`. A use the liveness walker cannot see makes the
# variable look DEAD at an earlier consuming position, so the value is MOVED
# instead of cloned and the later read returns garbage — or trips the GIR
# validator. Under-approximation is the dangerous direction here.
#
# Measured at pristine HEAD, 2026-08-27:
#   both -> ICE rc 101, `local _N read after MoveZero`, on a valid program.
#
# The payload is heap-forced via `mk` and long enough that a moved-from read
# is visibly garbage rather than accidentally intact.
String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s = mk("abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789", "ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ")
    Vector[String] v = []
    v.push(s)
    unsafe:
        print(s)
    String t = mk("0123456789012345678901234567890123456789", "abcdefghij")
    Vector[String] w = []
    w.push(t)
    zone:
        print(t)
